# 3. CGP program

A program written with a library works the same way, if the library builds for the web. This example is the
template project of [CGP](https://github.com/drohmer/cgp-2027), a C++ library made for teaching computer
graphics, compiled for the web without changing a line. The mouse turns the camera, its ImGui window stays
on screen, and the arrow keys still go to the slides.

